<title>USA: Liposome reacquires rights from Pfizer.</title>
<headline>Liposome reacquires rights from Pfizer.</headline>
<dateline>PRINCETON, N.J. 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Liposome Co said Tuesday that it has reacquired all development, manufacturing and marketing rights to TLC D-99, liposomal doxorubicin, which is currently being tested for metastatic breast cancer, from its developmental partner, Pfizer Inc.</p>
<p>Liposome said interim analyses of Phase III studies of the drug were positive.</p>
